-- title:
--   Finite idèle units of a maximal order with prescribed reduced norms
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q,q'$ be primes such that the quaternion algebra $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`, i.e. $a>0$ or $b>0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible precisely when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $B$ which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and every order containing it equals it. Let $\varepsilon$ assign to each height-one prime $w$ an element $\varepsilon_w$ of the completion $\mathbb{Q}_w$ with $v(\varepsilon_w)=1$, i.e. a unit of the valuation ring. Then there is a unit $u$ of $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in the stabiliser of the finite adèlic box of $\Lambda$ (the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adèle) such that for every $w$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ onto $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z\text{ read coordinatewise over }\mathbb{Q}_w)$, the reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}=x_0^2-ax_1^2-bx_2^2+abx_3^2$ of $\varphi$ applied to the $w$-component of $u$ equals $\varepsilon_w$.
--
--   This is the adèlic packaging of local surjectivity of the reduced norm from $\Lambda_w^\times$ onto the units $\mathbb{Z}_w^\times$ at every finite place, for a maximal order in an indefinite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ ramified exactly at two primes. It is used to produce elements of prescribed reduced norm in the associated adèlic and global settings, and is cited in the construction of right-multiplication identifications and in the existence statements for elements of reduced norm $\pm 1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_exists_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_forall_nrd_eq_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt.lean

